.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void csmp::TextInterface::OutputDataAsTextColumns (const \fBModel\fP< dim > & sg, const char * fname, const char * var) const"

.PP
single variable text column output Saves the values of a physical variable into a text output file\&. The first column in the output file gives you the unique ID number of each node, edge, face, interface or element depending where the specified variable has been defined\&. For node variables the coordinates of the nodes are supplied in the second and third column of the output file\&. For face, interface or element variables coordinates are also supplied in the second and third column\&. These coordinates refer to the centerpoint (barycentre) of each element\&. For integration points coordinates are given for each point\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
Outputs into a file named by the first argument string plus extension "\&.txt" the variable identified by the second string argument\&. An optional third argument allows you to append the timestep to the filename\&. This timestep information must be an integer\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void csmp::TextInterface::OutputRegionsToTextFiles (const \fBModel\fP< dim > & sg, const char * property) const"
Outputs a model property (distributed physical variable) into a series of text files with names corresponding to sub-regions of the model identified as groups\&. The resulting filenames are extended by a timestep integer and the '\&.txt' extension\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The name of the output property and the timestep which denotes the current state of the model\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Uses the method OutputRegionDataAsTextColumns()\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
The output text-column format is useful for a variety of plotting programs such as Texplot, Sigma Plot, SpyGlass Transform, Excel etc\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method will report an error and return without creating any output if no groups were defined\&. 
.SS "void csmp::TextInterface::ReadPixelTextImage256 (const char * fname, \fBMatrix\fP & data)"
Initialises the supplied matrix from file\&. 
.SS "void csmp::TextInterface::SizeofPixelTextImage256 (const char * fname, size_t & m, size_t & n)"
Appends a line to a textfile\&. This line will contain the current model time, the object-host ID of a physical variable (e\&.g\&., the node number of the node for which the variable value is output), and the variable value at specifically flagged host-object locations inside of a subregion of a CSMP model identified as a group object\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
AppendRegionToTextFileWhere() expects four arguments, the name of the textfile to which the output line shall be appended to, the name of the subregion of the model, the name of the property which shall be output to file, and the group-internal flag of the host-object for which the variable shall be output (either PLAIN or BOUNDARY)\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Calls the \fBRegion\fP class interface AppendToTextFileWhere()\&. 
.br
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
AppendRegionToTextFileWhere() allows the user to monitor property values in small subregions of a model over time\&. The resulting data can be visualized directly with Spyglass Plot, Excel or other programs\&. 
.br
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method will report an error and exit without completing its task, if the target group does not exist\&.

.PP
